comments[5]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-07-29T04:34:08.230Z","harness:claude-code","Duplicate check before create: pm-j8z6 owns reconciling the linked-file DATA after relocations and its acceptance criteria are about a tracker-only migration, not about how the check reports; pm-6olc95 owns the opposite scoping error on graph audit (active-only coverage that under-reports); pm-2ler is CLOSED and shipped exactly this partition for dependency_references, which is the precedent this item asks the files check to adopt; pm-chyh is CLOSED and covered path anchoring, not staleness reporting. Searched keyword and semantic for validate check gating, active holders, terminal informational, missing linked paths; grepped the corpus for missing_linked_paths holders. No existing item owns the reporting contract of the files check."
  "2026-09-05T16:12:56.029Z","harness:codex","negative controls reproduced two baseline failures: malformed multi-path references received moved/deleted inference, and terminal-only stale links kept the files check at warn. Implementing shared public SDK repair rows with lifecycle counters and bounded owners; no historical link mutation required."
  "2026-09-05T17:10:30.660Z","harness:codex","Live repaired corpus proof: 2642 items; active missing paths=0; active missing holder/field links=0; orphaned existing paths=0; historical missing links=1461 across195 paths, all closed. Nine active relocations were proven by git rename ancestry a5be2cda3, migrated through pm files on pm-92if/pm-7ob5/pm-szdc, and claims released. Historical ambiguity remains visible and is never auto-pruned."
  "2026-09-05T17:22:52.005Z","harness:codex","Strict token-budget gate caught validate --counts increasing to1778 tokens against an unchanged1758 ceiling. Added a negative regression for sparse false *_truncated markers while preserving true omission markers, false ordinary settings, and zero counts. The repair targets the shared counts projection rather than relaxing the mandatory budget."
  "2026-09-05T17:53:09.834Z","harness:codex","Final local evidence: 8457 tests across 617 files pass at exact 100% lines/statements/functions/branches (60094/62503/12956/47351 covered). Full quality:static passes, including unchanged token ceilings, docstrings, graph composition, and record integrity. Typecheck, version policy, ShellCheck, credential scan, zero-vulnerability dependency audit, and enforced Trivy scan pass. Final npm/npx and Bun/bunx packed smoke covers all 13 packages; separate temporary installed SDK/CLI acceptance passes. Required Sentry/telemetry gate passes with zero blocking Sentry groups and no failures lacking error codes. PR review and hosted checks are the remaining delivery stage."
notes[1]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-09-05T17:24:21.049Z","harness:codex","Architecture: pure linked-file lifecycle accounting lives in sdk/governance; validate owns filesystem collection and passes the resolved workspace registry. Paths and holder/field links are counted before projection. Compact and full outputs share row types, with explicit independent path/owner truncation."
